Game-Terminal

One command, game, for every terminal game in the Game namespace and
Term::Maze. On its own it draws a menu of the games and starts the one you
choose with the arrow keys, and shows the menu again when the game ends.
Given a name it starts that game at once, passing the rest of the command
line through, so game checkers --level 3 is checkers --level 3. Each game
runs inside the same process through its Terminal class's run method.

INSTALLATION

To install this module, run the following commands:

	perl Makefile.PL
	make
	make test
	make install

SUPPORT AND DOCUMENTATION

After installing, you can find documentation for this module with the
perldoc command.

    perldoc Game::Terminal
    perldoc game

You can also look for information at:

    RT, CPAN's request tracker (report bugs here)
        https://rt.cpan.org/NoAuth/Bugs.html?Dist=Game-Terminal

    Search CPAN
        https://metacpan.org/release/Game-Terminal


